@startuml
!include theme.iuml
title Public bootstrap — CSRF preparation without an account
hide footbox
autonumber
participant "Browser\nPublicSession / api.ts" as Browser
participant "public_access.py\nmiddleware + route functions" as Access
participant "state : PublicAccessState" as State
participant "rate_limits.throttle()\n<<function>>" as Limiter
activate Browser
Browser -> Access : GET /api/public/session\noptional camfranglais_public cookie
activate Access
Access -> State : limit(client address)
activate State
State -> State : workspace()
activate State
State --> State : lazily cached PublicWorkspaceStore
deactivate State
State -> Limiter : throttle(db, hashed IP key, 120, 60)
activate Limiter
Limiter --> State : window incremented, or RateLimitExceeded
deactivate Limiter
State --> Access : shared store, or explicit error
deactivate State
opt limit and storage initialization succeeded
  note over Access : use_workspace(store) binds dataset, coursework and ownership.\nAll bindings are reset when the request exits.
  Access -> Access : public_session(request)
  activate Access
  Access --> Access : reuse/generate opaque cookie;\nderive CSRF token and capabilities
  deactivate Access
end
Access --> Browser : 200 bootstrap + Set-Cookie, or 429/503/500
deactivate Access
opt valid public_read_only capabilities and token
  Browser -> Browser : configureSession(csrf_token)
  activate Browser
  Browser --> Browser : in-memory token ready; render App
  deactivate Browser
end
deactivate Browser
legend bottom
  Successful capabilities: analyze/save_tests=true; edit_collection/edit_grammar/edit_recordings=false.
  Cookie: HttpOnly, SameSite=Lax, Secure in production. It is CSRF state, not login or user identity.
  Rate-limit rows live in public-access.sqlite3; no auth.sqlite3 initialization or fake account is required.
  Health bypasses the shared limit; this sequence shows the default include_academic=true bootstrap.
endlegend
@enduml
